.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Alexei Kitaev showed that a 1D spinless p-wave superconductor hosts unpaired Majorana zero modes -- particles that are their own antiparticles -- localized at the two ends of an open chain, whenever the chemical potential satisfies |\mu| &lt; 2t. A pair of spatially separated Majoranas encodes one nonlocal fermionic degree of freedom immune to local perturbations, making the Kitaev chain the founding proposal for topologically protected quantum computation. kitaev_chain_hamiltonian gives the bulk (periodic) BdG Bloch Hamiltonian used to confirm the bulk gap stays open, and kitaev_chain_bdg_real_space builds the open chain that exposes the Majorana end modes directly in the spectrum -- plotted below as a real-space structure so the two end modes are visible directly on the chain rather than as an abstract site index.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/topology/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_kitaev_majorana_modes_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/topology/plot_kitaev_majorana_modes`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Kitaev Chain: Unpaired Majorana Zero Modes</div>
    </div>


